  "structure": {
    "block_count": 39,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your fall baby is bound to be affectionate, generous and oh so organized.",
        "text_sha256": "636b5772c63f68164a059c8b251106360c79806d4a3c9a6091d76d7abd03cfe9",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Just so you know, What to Expect may earn commissions from the links included on this page. All sales and prices are accurate at the time of publishing.",
        "text_sha256": "2750b2f7f70af35175aee67cfbb0c80bcc1fb148d5036cad7d83e80e1d0c55e9",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "October is here and the leaves are changing — and that means it's fall y’all. And one thing’s for sure, according to your October baby's birth flowers : This month will bring you a bright, calm child with a generous spirit.",
        "text_sha256": "b46fe80381174487c3c08a7c6add2c48c8157f5620f1ac1c8fd0c53dd22e6ccc",
        "word_count": 41
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What are the October birth flowers?",
        "text_sha256": "d56f4dd012322a2a3b5b89b3ea6c089b0c92f37dc85c09a99b2285f75bf4bca1",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you have an October baby, his birth flowers are the sunny marigold and the easy-going cosmos. You might associate this month more with pumpkin spice and flannel than flowers, but when it comes to predicting (or celebrating) your young one's personality, these October flowers offer some beautiful insight: a bright, well-rounded child, who draws others to him with his generous, calm nature.",
        "text_sha256": "877a369018b088c16437ea406fe863f2888134762ed56e0576beea29a7c3f529",
        "word_count": 63
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Marigold: A symbol of the rising sun",
        "text_sha256": "4974ec791300ba4bd7b455a2b3e0efd560f52653e4581d67cbaca49e263c3b02",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Marigolds in shades of radiant orange, yellow and red are the perfect fall flower, though they’ve been blooming all summer long (and will keep blooming until the first frost). Trusted SourceNC State ExtensionCalendula officinalisSee All Sources [1] While native to North, South and Central America, marigolds were already beloved around the world by the early 1600s. Shakespeare compared the opening and closing of marigolds to sunrise and sunset. Trusted SourceShakespeare Birthplace TrustShakespeare's Favourite Flowers: The MarigoldSee All Sources [2] For the Victorians (who popularized the language of flowers), marigolds were spiritual flowers, representing sacred affections, hope and charity. Trusted SourceFlora's Interpreter and Fortuna FloraMarigoldSee All Sources [3]",
        "text_sha256": "efb37c355a91552d0e37430a48a18a2129255af1197110579617704d6eb97d65",
        "word_count": 107
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceNC State ExtensionCalendula officinalisSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "7eb71c73381eeef40e1ccb46886987db5c89896590df922ae5823d17e3767e1c",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceShakespeare Birthplace TrustShakespeare's Favourite Flowers: The MarigoldSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "b1e14bc25d0efbc0dae7c807d32c79ba3c1ae3c18b4fca02555f5357083bfeeb",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceFlora's Interpreter and Fortuna FloraMarigoldSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "cfeee98ca4ece35a194535efa28b27037494a3462344ff81e52960e6af80de78",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You can expect your October baby to be as brilliant as the morning sun and as inspiring as the sunset. While the toddler years will definitely be a bit fiery (like those marigold petals!), with his deep affection and generosity, just knowing him is a never-ending gift.",
        "text_sha256": "fad19d9867937d3036081cbbfce6f64449802aa7f49c5725aadfc2f4b8346ece",
        "word_count": 47
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Cosmos: Balance in all things",
        "text_sha256": "e5ca7414d0bb6766e159b62afda32460a189f8ab06b74cb93954cc90d1f1a04e",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Cosmos are a favorite among gardeners because they're easy to grow and their warm-colored blooms are a surefire way to attract every butterfly and pollinator in town. Native to Central America, cosmos are mainly scentless except for one dark red variety that smells like chocolate (nothing wrong there!). Trusted SourceBritannica CosmosSee All Sources [4] Their name comes from the Greek kosmos meaning organized, balanced and whole — and what else could you desire for your little one? Trusted SourceUtah State University Cosmos in the GardenSee All Sources [5]",
        "text_sha256": "6a2ac6b25484914a571ee4978bace1054aa7ee070da1642b2f53dd0de03c825c",
        "word_count": 88
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Cosmos",
        "text_sha256": "168ae35c7276ff55bf80e6917cd758d1f7e73e8a6387801c3eecdbb067d5ce20",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceUtah State University Cosmos in the GardenSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "6d881c7cd042fa882fef21fca4a122d0e85a3158deaea0cbbe9826c0877d7563",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Cosmos children have great organizational skills (but you will have to wait and see whether it’s more about cleanliness or leadership). But perhaps most importantly, he will be known for his balanced, calm nature that will guide him through many of life’s challenges. A true joy in every way. Trusted SourceJstorThe Origins of Greek Kosmos and Latin MundusSee All Sources [6]",
        "text_sha256": "0304d5060f03869b05e6f9b04f3bcd730f74e3ec26b1828d7362c55425777b57",
        "word_count": 61
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceJstorThe Origins of Greek Kosmos and Latin MundusSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "25cc880c644894f46157a367674cc5353c3e0a44d487a7c8a0c59a6aca08b78d",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Incorporating marigolds and cosmos into your family's life",
        "text_sha256": "b1b05d3276a343d3c2c9f952292dc6ce071c0094c3b464cac8c7f0f9e6b41c27",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "It's easy to add your October baby's fiery birth flowers throughout your home or greenspace. These fun ideas are sure to add some pops of color — and personality! — to your everyday life:",
        "text_sha256": "ec8ec47380a882a744113d7edc79abd50b929418887e7ccd6f118f49c61f55c3",
        "word_count": 34
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Gather in the garden. Marigolds and cosmos are pollinators' best friends, but the marigold can also be beneficial to add to your garden, too. Their aromatic foliage attracts insect pests away from other tender flowers and vegetables while repelling chipmunks and squirrels.",
        "text_sha256": "9f86f3760cefddd58288411a0f9bcb47cbd6874dbab6bf4a028e43f37aa9be4f",
        "word_count": 42
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Build a boho bouquet. A bunch of fiery marigolds or lacy cosmos simply thrown in a vase make for great boho bouquets. It’s not just about the cheery, bright flowers but their intricate, lacy leaves. Want a fancier look? Check out the instructions for this cosmos and summer flower arrangement .",
        "text_sha256": "fea6ace026eb108f2a2f46ea2dcbf4834964e33d64f8a094a2c39b73f19050f1",
        "word_count": 51
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Experiment in the kitchen. Both marigolds and cosmos are edible — marigolds taste peppery while cosmos taste like nectar. Try marigolds in salads or as a garnish atop savory foods. Cosmos blooms make delightful pastry decorations . Cosmos cupcake decorating party, anyone?",
        "text_sha256": "7342e0dd792a02acfafec69dad9dfa3985977fc73c6bbbb8b6ea86ae56f065db",
        "word_count": 42
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Buy or DIY. Felt marigolds and cosmos make great everlasting bouquets, or you can combine them with felt beads for a beautiful mobile that will definitely keep your little one occupied. You can either make your own or head over to your nearest felt flower or crafting shop, a la Etsy !",
        "text_sha256": "a758ea65723eeb4810fdd26b375c39dcec9bb216d30c7bfa0abd724212bf6181",
        "word_count": 52
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Try creating a rust nursery that isn’t rusty! The rusty marigold yellow/orange has made a comeback in nursery decor (from the 70’s). Check out these nursery designs to fulfill all your decorating dreams.",
        "text_sha256": "10177be78bb8f7d4cadc59edb8652034ccc1c278c9069ab09582ad0bab1fa583",
        "word_count": 33
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Dye your heart out. Marigolds can be used to make a yellow-orange dye that is reminiscent of drops of sunshine. Dye onesies, bedsheets, curtains and more with this natural dye recipe or try out a marigold (or marigold-colored) tie-dye project together with your little one!",
        "text_sha256": "6074cd8f432b5b3d47bb177e9f7e1c4d240ce30a53985587b9a7a2743c8bdfaa",
        "word_count": 45
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Looking for more fun insights about your baby? Discover the astrological traits of your baby with our free Birth Chart Calculator .",
        "text_sha256": "c863c6e279b90aa2b869ed7ed1f595b2b9decf9af9e26f88a6efd7692de37f27",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Sources",
        "text_sha256": "caf85b0888d78f1f83771a07b25c3d30fa1210242f2fae6e5ae5d9a686602800",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Calendula officinalis",
        "text_sha256": "f833b96db89040bd2750d685d79318f90af34fa9b2fae7adbdff334ac76dbec3",
        "word_count": 2
      },
